==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*surma}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*śurma}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|fi|surra|ma|id2=nominal}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|surm}}, {{cog|krl|šurma}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[violent]] [[death]], mainly used of humans.
#: ''He saivat surmansa'' = They got killed (literally: “they got their deaths”).
# [[personification|Personification]] of sudden [[death]].
#: ''Hän joutui '''surman''' suuhun'' = He got killed (literally: "he got into the mouth of death'").
# {{lb|fi|legal}} [[killing|Killing]], [[voluntary]] [[manslaughter]] under [[mitigating]] circumstances.

====Usage notes====
* (''law'') ''Killing'' is the ''unofficial'' translation of Finnish penal code used by the Ministry of Justice of Finland. See usage notes under {{m|fi|tappo}}.

